# Terraform Conventions

## Version Constraints
- Terraform: `required_version = ">= 1.9"`
- AWS provider: `required_providers { aws = { source = "hashicorp/aws", version = "~> 6.0" } }`

## Provider Configuration
- Always use `profile = var.aws_profile` (default `"charteracademy"`)
- Always use `region = var.region` (default `"af-south-1"`)
- Apply `default_tags` block on the provider for Project, Environment, ManagedBy tags:
```hcl
default_tags {
  tags = {
    Project     = var.project_name
    Environment = var.environment
    ManagedBy   = "terraform"
  }
}
```

## Module Structure
Each module directory contains: `main.tf`, `variables.tf`, `outputs.tf`

## Naming
- All identifiers use `snake_case`
- Resource names prefixed with `local.name_prefix` (`"${var.project_name}-${var.environment}"`)

## AMIs
- Never hardcode AMI IDs -- always use `aws_ami` data source with `owners = ["amazon"]` filter

## Variables
- Every variable must have `description`, `type`, and `validation` blocks where appropriate

## Sensitive Outputs
- Mark with `sensitive = true`

## Remote State
- S3 backend (versioned, encrypted) + DynamoDB lock table, both in af-south-1
- `.terraform.lock.hcl` must always be committed to version control

## Pre-commit Checks
- Run `terraform fmt` and `terraform validate` before every commit
